meta {
  name: Remove a member
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/members/:member?mode=reserve
  body: none
  auth: bearer
}

params:query {
  mode: reserve
}

params:path {
  member: john
}

headers {
  ~Idempotency-Key: replace-with-a-unique-key
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{token}}
}

docs {
  Offboards the member: memberships, roles, delegations, rooms and device credentials they approved are revoked. With `mode=reserve` (default) the address is held for a successor (invite someone to the same handle); the old mailbox keeps its history, detached from the org. `mode=delete` releases the address.

  Scope: `members:write`.

  Errors: `unauthorized` (401), `ip_not_allowed` (403), `insufficient_scope` (403), `forbidden` (403), `not_found` (404), `feature_disabled` (404), `org_inactive` (409), `org_read_only` (409), `idempotency_conflict` (409), `rate_limited` (429), `store_error` (500).
}
